    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as the clear offensive anchor. With a score of 78.53, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** provides the highest ceiling of the active lineup, bolstered by a favorable 4.33 xERA matchup against Rod\u00f3n and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates his base projection by 7%. **Josh Lowe** also emerges as a high-upside play at 70.14, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Severino, L. While **Josh Lowe**\u2019s speed is a premium asset in our strategy, the 14% boost from his dynamic platoon and the 14% lift from the opposing SP skill underscore why he remains a foundational start today. **Nolan Schanuel** rounds out the top tier at 59.81, leveraging a solid spot in the order and a favorable 4.60 xERA opponent to provide stability in the middle of our lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the daily optimizer involved **Liam Hicks** and **Nasim Nunez**, both of whom occupy the \"Marginal\" territory of our efficiency scale. While **Liam Hicks** (52.47) managed to secure a spot due to his high placement in the order against Strider, **Nasim Nunez** (49.48) struggled to clear the threshold; his elite sprint speed\u2014typically a primary driver for our roster selection\u2014could not overcome the drag of the #8 batting position and the neutral-to-negative impact of the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time. Consequently, **Nasim Nunez** remains a start only due to a lack of deeper alternatives today. Regarding our bench, the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill** due to team off-days has forced a leaner lineup, while the continued IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.** remains the most significant drag on our overall stolen base efficiency. Managers should monitor weather updates for the games featuring **Dominic Smith** (53.85), as any precipitation could further dampen his already modest output against Alcantara, S.",
